   240	**Trade-offs:**
   241	- (+) Uses existing hook, semantically correct ("after effects processed, wait for them to settle")
   242	- (+) Keeps module logic in `supportJsModules.js`
   243	- (-) Making `onEffect` async could have unintended consequences for other `onEffect` listeners
   244	- (-) Changes the documented hook contract (though the docs describe `onEffect` as "After effects processed" which is vague)
   245	
   246	### Option B: Make `invokeOnMorph` run callbacks sequentially
   247	
   248	Change `invokeOnMorph` from `Promise.all` to sequential execution (in registration order). Then ensure `supportJsModules.js` registers its `onMorph` callback before `supportMorphDom.js` by importing it first in `features/index.js`.
   249	
   250	**Trade-offs:**
   251	- (+) No new hooks needed
   252	- (-) Relies on import order in `features/index.js`, which is fragile
   253	- (-) Sequential execution of all `onMorph` callbacks could be slower than parallel
   254	- (-) Semantically confusing: the module loading step isn't really "morphing"
   255	
